BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beads to Jewelry - October
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTSTAMP:20261025T143341Z
UID:64da68c89ede4bb9a5e81bea28eb@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Turn Handmade Glass Beads into Wearable Art You've created bea
 utiful beads—now it's time to transform them into stunning\, wearable je
 welry. In this hands-on workshop\, professional glass and metal jeweler Am
 anda will guide students through the process of designing and assembling f
 inished jewelry using lampworked glass beads. Whether you've spent the pas
 t few months filling your bead collection in our flameworking classes or y
 ou're completely new to lampworked beads\, this class is for you. You do n
 ot need to have made your own beads to participate. Students are welcome t
 o bring beads they've created\, use beads they've collected elsewhere\, or
  purchase handmade lampworked beads from the studio on the day of class. T
 hroughout the workshop\, students will learn how to thoughtfully combine g
 lass beads with metal findings\, accent beads\, and wire elements to creat
 e balanced\, professional-quality jewelry. Amanda will demonstrate a varie
 ty of finishing techniques while discussing design\, proportion\, color ba
 lance\, and the hardware that transforms individual beads into elegant nec
 klaces\, bracelets\, and earrings. Some larger-hole beads may be fitted wi
 th sterling silver cores for a refined\, finished appearance\, while other
 s can be ground and prepared for assembly using head pins\, eye pins\, wir
 e wrapping\, and decorative metal accents. Students will also explore simp
 le wire embellishments that add both beauty and structural support to thei
 r finished pieces. By the end of class\, you'll leave wearing—or ready t
 o gift—a one-of-a-kind piece of jewelry featuring handcrafted glass bead
 s assembled with professional techniques. Students Will Learn Basic jewelr
 y design principles and composition Selecting complementary beads and meta
 l findings Using head pins\, eye pins\, jump rings\, and wire components C
 reating balanced necklaces\, bracelets\, or earrings Incorporating decorat
 ive wire details When and how to use sterling silver bead cores Preparing 
 lampworked beads for jewelry assembly Professional finishing techniques fo
 r durable\, wearable jewelry No Previous Beadmaking Experience Required Th
 is class is open to everyone! While it's the perfect follow-up for student
 s who have completed our lampworking bead classes\, you do not need to hav
 e made your own beads to participate. We offer a beautiful selection of ha
 ndmade lampworked glass beads available for purchase during class\, making
  it easy to create a unique piece of jewelry even if this is your very fir
 st visit. Studio-made beads are available for $3 each and may be purchased
  on the day of class. Students are also welcome to bring their own handmad
 e beads or favorite specialty beads from home. Whether you're preserving m
 emories from your beadmaking journey or simply looking for a fun introduct
 ion to jewelry design\, this class is a wonderful way to transform beautif
 ul glass into finished pieces you'll treasure for years to come. This is a
  5 hour class. It is for students 12 and up. Max 8 students per class.\n\n
 Source: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/beads-to-jewelry-october/11
 1447/
LOCATION:Blackstone River Glass Center\, 30 Meeting Street\, Cumberland\, 
 RI 20864
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/beads-to-jewelry-october/111447
 /
END:VEVENT
